<% provide(:title, "How It Works") %>

<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9">
      <span class="smb-b2b-pill mb-2">
        <i class="fas fa-cogs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>Zero Physical Handover · 100% Digital PNR Settlement</span>
      </span>
      <h1 class="h2 mb-3">How ShareMyBag Airline Exchange Works</h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted mb-5">
        Instead of strangers handing physical parcels at airports, ShareMyBag lets an airline run a live Bid/Ask exchange for <strong>digital baggage allowance</strong> inside each commercial flight between T-48h and T-4h before departure.
      </p>

      <div class="row g-4 mb-5">
        <div class="col-md-4">
          <div class="smb-card p-4 h-100">
            <div class="smb-step-number mb-3" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
            <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Verified Flight PNR</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
              Only ticketed passengers booked on the exact same flight can enter its order book. Each passenger's PNR allowance (typically 23 kg) is verified against the aircraft's certified baggage envelope.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
          <div class="smb-card p-4 h-100">
            <div class="smb-step-number mb-3" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
            <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Bid / Ask Matching</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
              Light travelers post ASK orders for unused kg; heavy travelers post BID orders for exact extra kg. Our Price-Time Priority engine supports instant fractional fills at the resting maker price.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
          <div class="smb-card p-4 h-100">
            <div class="smb-step-number mb-3" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
            <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Atomic PNR &amp; Revenue</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
              Both PNRs update atomically (e.g., 23→13 kg and 23→33 kg), the seller receives instant airline flight voucher credit, and the carrier books a 25% ancillary margin with zero extra check-in friction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="smb-card p-4 mb-4" aria-labelledby="compliance-heading">
        <h2 id="compliance-heading" class="h4 mb-3">Why Airport Security, Customs &amp; Airlines Approve This Model</h2>
        <div class="row g-3">
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h3 class="h6 text-dark">Airport Security (DGAC / TSA / ICAO Annex 17)</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
              Passengers never carry someone else's items. Every traveler packs, secures, and checks only their own suitcase — eliminating the "unaccompanied or unknown third-party item" prohibition completely.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h3 class="h6 text-dark">Customs &amp; Border Liability</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
              Each traveler remains 100% legally responsible for the contents of their own personal luggage. Only digital weight entitlement on the carrier's reservation system is reallocated.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h3 class="h6 text-dark">Aircraft Weight &amp; Balance Safety</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
              Every trade transfers weight 1:1 inside the aircraft's certified baggage payload cap and closes strictly at <strong>T-4h</strong> before departure so loadsheets are finalized normally.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <h3 class="h6 text-dark">IATA 32 kg Single-Bag Health Limit</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
              A passenger's PNR allowance can scale up to <strong>46 kg</strong>, while preserving the mandatory <strong>32 kg maximum per individual bag</strong> (split across 2 pieces above 32 kg).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <%= link_to "Explore Live Flight Order Books", flights_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
        <%= link_to "Inspect Airline ROI & Fleet Simulator", airline_roi_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
